        <p>ALL LADIES will be glad to bear that Mrs. M. Darnerau, CERTIFICATED MIDWIFE, has a safe anel certain mixture for obstructions and irregularities, which she will send, post free, for 4s. 9d. It is absolutely guaranteed, even in long-steoading obstinate eases. It cannot fail, and is perfectly harmless. Do not trust In bogus advertisements of quacks and other ignorant People, they never send lon the right remedy. If you have already done so, send for this Mixture as a last resource and Aou will not be deceived. You will find that it is always cheaper to come to the right place first. Below are some testimonials received. The originals of these, with thousands of others, can be seen any time. Fr .m Mn. Chetharn : " Madam, will you kindly send again one bottle of your Female Mixture, as the last acted splendidly. I enclose Ac."—Mrs. Binnte writes : " Kindly lorward by return of at a bottle of your Female Mixture. It Out me all right last olme, and I trust it will do BO again." —From Mrs. "fetcher t 'Madame. I received the Mixture all right, and I took the doses as stated ; it did all that was needed, for which I thank you very much."—Mrs. S. writes from Sheffield : "I am pleased to tell you your medicine did all bat was required, though I thought it had failed, for I had the last dose thirty hours before any change took place. I had the last dose on Sunday, and all was right as possible Tuesday aftelnoon. Everything had been as Well as It was possible. Had I written t 'you at first, I should have been over £2 in pocket. You may show this ,etter, but cover name and address."—Mrs. Bryan writs: "Madam. I am glad to be able to report that th- last two doses have had the desired effect. I shall r commend your remedy to all my married friends. I think it ,s excellent, and should I be in difficulty again myself, shouldat once apply to you." —From Mrs Carside "I have muo b pLasure in sending you news of having relief the first morn' ng, for which lam very thankful indeed. I shall always fee_ grateful for your Mixture, and if I need anything again. .vill send to you." Address Miss. DAMIIRAC, Milton Cottage, Forest Bill. London</p>
